From eabd09f3fc02b32f6b990066cc732992396403ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baris Dinc <barisdinc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:51:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] library: axi_datv_xpdr: Add an NCO shifted beacon path

Add a second TX source next to the repeater: the DMA/interpolator data is
shifted by an NCO and added to the repeater output with saturation, so a
locally generated signal (DVB-S2 beacon) can be transmitted in the same
channel as the relayed one.

The NCO uses a quarter wave sine table in block RAM, addressed with the
12 MSBs of a 32-bit phase accumulator (spurs below -72 dBc), and a complex
mixer on 4 DSP slices. A CORDIC was tried first but needs ~1500 LUTs,
which do not fit into the Zynq-7010 next to the Pluto design.

New registers:
  0x040 CONTROL     [3] beacon enable
  0x054 BEACON_FREQ NCO phase increment, f = fs * n / 2^32 (signed)
  0x080 STATUS      [2] beacon enable

The squelch and the force mute only act on the repeater path. With both
paths disabled the DMA data is passed through unchanged as before. A new
tx_valid input advances the NCO once per DAC sample.
